From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] soc/intel/skylake: Don't access MSR_BIOS_DONE

With MAINBOARD_SUPPORTS_COFFEELAKE_CPU, cpu_soc_is_in_untrusted_mode()
reads MSR_BIOS_DONE (0x151). A Coffee Lake CPU on a 100/200-series
board, such as the i3-9100T in a Dell OptiPlex 3050, doesn't have it,
and the read raises #GP.

Until SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_GPIO_LOCK_USING_SBI was selected for
Skylake, nothing called the function. Now gpio_non_smm_lock_pad() calls
it for every pad locked from the ramstage pad tables, and ramstage
halts:

  CPU Index 0 - APIC 0 Unexpected Exception:13 @ 08:7aa47cb3 - Halting
  ...
  eax: 7aa87540 ebx: 7aa87540 ecx: 00000151 edx: 00000000

The mode can never be on here: only cpu_soc_bios_done() enables it, and
on this SoC nothing calls cpu_soc_bios_done() (only Alder Lake and
Meteor Lake call before_post_cpus_init()). Return false without reading
the MSR, as Skylake and Kaby Lake CPUs already got. Make
cpu_soc_bios_done() a no-op too, so that a future caller can't raise
the same #GP, and drop the now unused MSR definitions.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/skylake/cpu.c             | 21 +++++----------------
 src/soc/intel/skylake/include/soc/msr.h |  3 ---
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/skylake/cpu.c b/src/soc/intel/skylake/cpu.c
index 9c82565784..e02f87815f 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/skylake/cpu.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/skylake/cpu.c
@@ -30,27 +30,16 @@
 bool cpu_soc_is_in_untrusted_mode(void)
 {
 	/*
-	 * TODO: Add dynamic detection to identify if skylake SoC
-	 * is in coffeelake board.
+	 * cpu_soc_bios_done() never enables the mode on this SoC. Don't read
+	 * MSR_BIOS_DONE to find out: Coffee Lake CPUs on 100/200-series boards
+	 * don't have it and raise #GP.
 	 */
-	if (!CONFIG(MAINBOARD_SUPPORTS_COFFEELAKE_CPU))
-		return false;
-
-	/* IA_UNTRUSTED_MODE is not supported in Sky Lake */
-	msr_t msr = rdmsr(MSR_BIOS_DONE);
-	return !!(msr.lo & ENABLE_IA_UNTRUSTED);
+	return false;
 }
 
+/* IA untrusted mode isn't supported here, see above. */
 void cpu_soc_bios_done(void)
 {
-	if (!CONFIG(MAINBOARD_SUPPORTS_COFFEELAKE_CPU))
-		return;
-
-	msr_t msr;
-
-	msr = rdmsr(MSR_BIOS_DONE);
-	msr.lo |= ENABLE_IA_UNTRUSTED;
-	wrmsr(MSR_BIOS_DONE, msr);
 }
 
 /* Read on the BSP before the APs start, since soc_core_init() runs on every core */
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/skylake/include/soc/msr.h b/src/soc/intel/skylake/include/soc/msr.h
index a495799e9b..92e8215567 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/skylake/include/soc/msr.h
+++ b/src/soc/intel/skylake/include/soc/msr.h
@@ -5,9 +5,6 @@
 
 #include <intelblocks/msr.h>
 
-/* IA_UNTRUSTED_MODE is not supported in Sky Lake */
-#define MSR_BIOS_DONE		0x151
-#define  ENABLE_IA_UNTRUSTED	(1 << 0)
 #define MSR_LT_LOCK_MEMORY		0x2e7
 #define MSR_UNCORE_PRMRR_PHYS_BASE	0x2f4
 #define MSR_UNCORE_PRMRR_PHYS_MASK	0x2f5
